IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ohs-dates`

-- Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004 (Vic), Version No. 045 (6 August 2025) -- seat-neutral core.
--
-- The general duties of Part 3 (ss 20-34), consultation (s 35), incidents (Part 5, ss 37-39), workplace manslaughter
-- (Part 5A, ss 39B-39G with s 187), the cease-work and issue-resolution steps a worker meets (ss 74, 75), discrimination
-- for raising health and safety (Part 7 Division 9, ss 76-78E), and the offence machinery around them (ss 131, 132,
-- 139, 144, 145, 148A, 148B, 152) with the penalty of every offence in scope.
--
-- Conventions (the 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 rulings, NOTES.md): JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own
-- words ("if", "only if", "while", "means", a flat negative, a period the text fixes); NOTHING where it is silent or a
-- grant is limited in its own wording. Judgments the Act leaves to a court or an inspector ("reasonably practicable",
-- "reasonable care", "negligent", "dominant reason", "substantial reason", "reasonable time") are inputs, never decided.
-- Penalties are in penalty units: the value of a penalty unit (Monetary Units Act 2004) is not deposited.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004 -- core`

§§ `Who is who (ss 5, 5A)`

-- s 5(1) "employee means a person employed under a contract of employment or contract of training"; s 5A(1) a
-- worker a labour hire provider supplies to, recruits for or places with a person is taken to be that person's
-- employee, unless the regulations exclude the person or the worker (s 5A(2), (3); the regulations are not deposited,
-- so the exclusion is a fact).
GIVEN `employed under a contract of employment or training` IS A BOOLEAN
      `supplied, recruited or placed by a labour hire provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `excluded by the regulations from s 5A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an employee of the employer (ss 5, 5A)` IF
        `employed under a contract of employment or training`
    OR  (`supplied, recruited or placed by a labour hire provider` AND (NOT `excluded by the regulations from s 5A`))

§§ `Part 3 -- the concept of ensuring health and safety (s 20)`

-- s 20(1): a duty to ensure, so far as is reasonably practicable, health and safety requires the person (a) to
-- eliminate risks so far as reasonably practicable, and (b) if that is not reasonably practicable, to reduce them so far
-- as reasonably practicable. What is reasonably practicable (s 20(2): likelihood, harm, knowledge, availability, cost)
-- is a judgment for the court, so each limb is an input.
GIVEN `the risk was eliminated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `eliminating the risk was reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 20 standard is met` IF
        `the risk was eliminated`
    OR  ((NOT `eliminating the risk was reasonably practicable`) AND `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable`)

§§ `Part 3 -- to whom the employer's duties are owed (ss 21(3), 23)`

-- s 21(1)-(2) are owed to "employees of the employer"; s 21(3)(a) a reference to an employee includes an independent
-- contractor engaged by the employer and the contractor's employees, and (b) extends the duties to them "in relation to
-- matters over which the employer has control or would have control if not for any agreement purporting to limit or
-- remove that control".
-- JUST TRUE: an employee (ss 5, 5A), or a contractor (or its employee) on a matter within the employer's control.
-- NOTHING: a contractor on a matter outside that control (a scope limit in the text's own words, no "only").
-- JUST FALSE: neither an employee nor a contractor ("employee means"); s 23 then may apply.
GIVEN `is an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is an independent contractor engaged by the employer, or an employee of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is within the employer's control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the s 21 duty is owed (s 21(3))` MEANS
    IF `is an employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `is an independent contractor engaged by the employer, or an employee of one`
         THEN IF `the matter is within the employer's control`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 21(2): "Without limiting subsection (1), an employer contravenes that subsection if the employer fails to do any of
-- the following" (a)-(e). Each failure is judged "so far as is reasonably practicable" or "as is necessary", so each is
-- an input. s 152: a person who complies with regulations or a compliance code that provide for the duty is taken to
-- have complied with it.
-- JUST TRUE: a failure under s 21(2), or the working environment not safe by the s 20 standard.
-- JUST FALSE: the duty was owed and met, or s 152 deems it met.
-- NOTHING: the duty is not shown to be owed (s 21(3) scope).
GIVEN `the duty is owed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `complied with regulations or a compliance code for the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `failed (a) safe plant or systems of work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `failed (b) safe use, handling, storage or transport of plant or substances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `failed (c) a safe workplace under its management and control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `failed (d) adequate welfare facilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `failed (e) necessary information, instruction, training or supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the working environment met the s 20 standard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer contravened s 21(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the duty is owed`
    WHEN JUST `owed` THEN
        IF NOT `owed`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF `complied with regulations or a compliance code for the duty`
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE IF     `failed (a) safe plant or systems of work`
                      OR `failed (b) safe use, handling, storage or transport of plant or substances`
                      OR `failed (c) a safe workplace under its management and control`
                      OR `failed (d) adequate welfare facilities`
                      OR `failed (e) necessary information, instruction, training or supervision`
                      OR (NOT `the working environment met the s 20 standard`)
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 23(1): an employer must ensure, so far as is reasonably practicable, that persons other than its employees are not
-- exposed to risks to their health or safety arising from the conduct of its undertaking. The duty is owed to a person
-- who is not the employer's employee (s 39F(2): the class is express); whether the risk arises from the conduct of the
-- undertaking is a fact.
-- JUST TRUE: owed and the s 20 standard not met (and s 152 not met). JUST FALSE: met, or s 152.
-- NOTHING: the person is the employer's employee (s 21, not s 23, speaks to them) or the risk did not arise from the
-- undertaking (the text is silent on such risks).
GIVEN `the person is an employee of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk arose from the conduct of the employer's undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `complied with regulations or a compliance code for the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the s 20 standard was met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer contravened s 23(1)` MEANS
    IF `the person is an employee of the employer` OR (NOT `the risk arose from the conduct of the employer's undertaking`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `complied with regulations or a compliance code for the duty` OR `the s 20 standard was met`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 3 -- the employee's own duties (s 25)`

-- s 25(1) "While at work, an employee must" (a) take reasonable care for their own health and safety, (b) take
-- reasonable care for others who may be affected, (c) co-operate with the employer's compliance; s 25(2) not
-- intentionally or recklessly interfere with or misuse anything provided for health, safety or welfare. Reasonable care is
-- judged having regard to what the employee knew (s 25(3)): an input.
-- JUST FALSE when not at work ("while" is a condition) or when every limb was kept.
GIVEN `at work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `failed to take reasonable care for my own health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN
      `failed to take reasonable care for others my acts or omissions may affect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `failed to co-operate with the employer's compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `intentionally or recklessly interfered with or misused safety equipment or facilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employee contravened s 25` MEANS
    IF NOT `at work`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF     `failed to take reasonable care for my own health and safety`
             OR `failed to take reasonable care for others my acts or omissions may affect`
             OR `failed to co-operate with the employer's compliance`
             OR `intentionally or recklessly interfered with or misused safety equipment or facilities`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 32: a person who, without lawful excuse, recklessly engages in conduct that places or may place another person at a
-- workplace in danger of serious injury is guilty of an indictable offence. Each element is an input.
GIVEN `had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `engaged in the conduct recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct placed or may have placed another person at a workplace in danger of serious injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the s 32 offence is made out` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `had a lawful excuse`)
       AND `engaged in the conduct recklessly`
       AND `the conduct placed or may have placed another person at a workplace in danger of serious injury`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 4 -- consultation (s 35)`

DECLARE `Consultation matter` IS ONE OF
    `identifying or assessing hazards or risks`
    `deciding measures to control risks`
    `deciding the adequacy of welfare facilities`
    `deciding procedures for resolving issues, consulting, monitoring, or information and training`
    `determining the membership of a health and safety committee`
    `proposing changes to the workplace, plant, substances or conduct of work that may affect health or safety`
    `a thing prescribed by the regulations`
    `something else`

-- s 35(1): when doing any of (a)-(g), an employer must so far as reasonably practicable consult the employees "who are
-- or are likely to be directly affected". (g) delegates to regulations not deposited: answered as a fact.
-- JUST TRUE: a listed matter and the employee is or is likely to be directly affected.
-- NOTHING: another matter (the list is closed only by (g), a delegation not deposited -- see fork F5) or an employee not
-- directly affected (a scope limit with no "only").
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Consultation matter`
      `directly affected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer must consult the employee (s 35(1))` MEANS
    IF NOT `directly affected`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the matter`
         WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 5 -- incidents (ss 37-39)`

DECLARE `Incident outcome` IS ONE OF
    `a death`
    `medical treatment needed within 48 hours of exposure to a substance`
    `immediate treatment as a hospital in-patient`
    `immediate medical treatment for an amputation, serious head or eye injury, de-gloving or scalping, electric shock, spinal injury, loss of a bodily function or serious lacerations`
    `serious risk from an immediate or imminent exposure to an escape, spillage or leakage of a substance`
    `serious risk from an immediate or imminent exposure to an implosion, explosion or fire`
    `serious risk from an immediate or imminent exposure to electric shock`
    `serious risk from an immediate or imminent exposure to the fall or release from a height of plant, a substance or a thing`
    `serious risk from an immediate or imminent exposure to the collapse, overturning, failure or malfunction of prescribed or registered-design plant`
    `serious risk from an immediate or imminent exposure to the collapse of a building, structure, excavation or mine, or shoring`
    `serious risk from an immediate or imminent exposure to an inrush of water, mud or gas, or loss of main ventilation, in a mine, underground excavation or tunnel`
    `an injury, consequence, event, circumstance or illness prescribed by the regulations`
    `none of these`

-- s 37: "This Part applies to an incident that results in" (1)(a)-(e), "also applies to" exposures (2)(a)-(j) and
-- prescribed illness (2A); (3) "Despite ..., this Part does not apply to an incident of a kind excluded by the
-- regulations". The heads that delegate to the regulations are asked as facts. JUST FALSE for none of the heads (a
-- list the text closes by handing the rest to the regulations: the delegated-definition ruling (a)) or an excluded kind.
GIVEN `the outcome` IS AN `Incident outcome`
      `excluded by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 5 applies to the incident (s 37)` IF
        (NOT `excluded by the regulations`)
    AND CONSIDER `the outcome`
        WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 38(1)-(2): an employer or self-employed person must notify the Authority immediately after becoming aware that an
-- incident has occurred at a workplace under its management and control; "However", not if it is the only person
-- injured, harmed or exposed. JUST FALSE where Part 5 does not apply, the workplace is not under its management and
-- control, it is not aware (the duty runs from awareness), or s 38(2) applies.
GIVEN `Part 5 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at a workplace under its management and control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `aware the incident occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was the only person harmed or exposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the incident must be notified (s 38(1), (2))` IF
        `Part 5 applies`
    AND `at a workplace under its management and control`
    AND `aware the incident occurred`
    AND (NOT `it was the only person harmed or exposed`)

DECLARE `Record inspector` IS ONE OF
    `a person injured in the incident, or exposed to serious risk by it`
    `a representative of a person injured or exposed`
    `a representative of a person whose death the incident caused`
    `a health and safety representative for my designated work group`
    `a member of the employer's health and safety committee`
    `someone else`

-- s 38(4): the record must be kept for at least 5 years and made available for inspection by (a) an inspector, (b) a
-- person injured or whose health or safety was exposed to serious risk, or their representative, (c) a representative of
-- a person whose death the incident caused, (d) for an employer only, the health and safety representative of a
-- designated work group the employees are in, and the members of its health and safety committees.
-- JUST TRUE within 60 months of the record being given (s 38(3)); JUST FALSE after (a period the text fixes, fork F3);
-- NOTHING for someone outside the list (a limit on the duty in its own wording) or (d) asked of a self-employed person.
GIVEN `who asks` IS A `Record inspector`
      `the duty-holder is an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record was given on` IS A DATE
      `the day of asking` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the record must be made available (s 38(4))` MEANS
    IF `the day of asking` `is after` (`the day` 60 `months after` `the record was given on`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `who asks`
         WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING
         WHEN `a health and safety representative for my designated work group` THEN
              IF `the duty-holder is an employer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `a member of the employer's health and safety committee` THEN
              IF `the duty-holder is an employer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 39: a duty-holder required to notify must not, without reasonable excuse, fail to ensure the site is not disturbed
-- until (a) an inspector arrives or (b) another time an inspector directs when notified; "Despite subsection (1)" (2) the
-- site may be disturbed to protect health or safety, aid an injured person, or take essential action to make it safe.
-- JUST TRUE: (2) applies, or the inspector has arrived or the directed time has come. JUST FALSE: the site must stay
-- undisturbed ("until"). NOTHING: no duty to notify, so s 39 does not speak.
GIVEN `the incident must be notified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an inspector has arrived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time an inspector directed has come` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to protect health or safety, aid an injured person, or make the site safe` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the site may be disturbed (s 39)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the incident must be notified`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `to protect health or safety, aid an injured person, or make the site safe`
             OR `an inspector has arrived`
             OR `the time an inspector directed has come`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 5A -- workplace manslaughter (ss 39B-39G, 187)`

DECLARE `Part 3 duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 21 duty to employees`
    `s 22 duty to monitor health and conditions`
    `s 23 duty to other persons`
    `s 24 self-employed person's duty`
    `s 25 employee's duty`
    `s 26 duty of a person who manages or controls a workplace`
    `s 27 duty of a designer of plant`
    `s 28 duty of a designer of buildings or structures`
    `s 29 duty of a manufacturer of plant or substances`
    `s 30 duty of a supplier of plant or substances`
    `s 31 duty of an installer of plant`
    `s 32 duty not to recklessly endanger`

-- s 39B "applicable duty means a duty imposed by a provision of Part 3 other than (a) the duty imposed by section 25; or
-- (b) a duty imposed by section 32 on a person who is an employee, but not an officer, at the workplace".
GIVEN `the duty` IS A `Part 3 duty`
      `the duty-holder is an employee and not an officer at the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an applicable duty (s 39B)` IF
    CONSIDER `the duty`
    WHEN `s 25 employee's duty` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 32 duty not to recklessly endanger` THEN NOT `the duty-holder is an employee and not an officer at the workplace`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 39E(1): conduct is negligent if it involves (a) a great falling short of the standard of care a reasonable person
-- (for a body corporate, a reasonable body corporate: (2)(d)) would have taken, and (b) a high risk of death, serious
-- injury or serious illness. Both are judgments: inputs.
GIVEN `a great falling short of the standard of care` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a high risk of death, serious injury or serious illness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is negligent (s 39E)` IF
    `a great falling short of the standard of care` AND `a high risk of death, serious injury or serious illness`

-- s 39F: A owes an applicable duty to B if Part 3 imposes it on A and B is, explicitly or implicitly, a person to whom it
-- is owed. Whether B belongs to the class the provision names (explicit) or whose health and safety it is meant to
-- ensure (implicit) is asked as a fact.
GIVEN `the duty` IS A `Part 3 duty`
      `the duty-holder is an employee and not an officer at the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased belonged to the class the duty is owed to or protects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owes an applicable duty to the deceased (s 39F)` IF
        `is an applicable duty (s 39B)` `the duty` `the duty-holder is an employee and not an officer at the workplace`
    AND `the deceased belonged to the class the duty is owed to or protects`

-- Part 5A was inserted on 1 July 2020 (No. 50/2019 ss 3-8, commencement in the endnotes). s 187(1): it applies to
-- offences alleged to have been committed on or after that insertion; (2) an offence alleged between two dates, one
-- before and one after, is alleged to have been committed before. So the conduct must have begun on or after
-- 1 July 2020.
`the day Part 5A was inserted` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2020

GIVEN `the conduct began on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 5A applies to the conduct (s 187)` IF
    `the day Part 5A was inserted` `is no later than` `the conduct began on`

-- s 39G(1): a person who is not a volunteer must not engage in conduct that (a) is negligent, (b) constitutes a breach
-- of an applicable duty the person owes to another person, and (c) causes that person's death. s 39G(2): the same for an
-- officer of an applicable entity (a body corporate, unincorporated body or association, or partnership, s 39G(3)) and
-- a duty the entity owes. JUST FALSE whenever an element fails (a flat prohibition: the section is not contravened on
-- these facts).
GIVEN `the conduct began on` IS A DATE
      `is a volunteer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct is negligent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct breached the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the duty is an applicable duty owed to the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct caused the death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39G is contravened` MEANS
    IF     `Part 5A applies to the conduct (s 187)` `the conduct began on`
       AND (NOT `is a volunteer`)
       AND `the conduct is negligent`
       AND `the conduct breached the duty`
       AND `the duty is an applicable duty owed to the deceased`
       AND `the conduct caused the death`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Unsafe work: cease work and the inspector (ss 73-75)`

DECLARE `Who directs` IS ONE OF
    `the employer`
    `the health and safety representative for the designated work group`
    `someone else`

-- s 74(1): if (a) an issue concerning health or safety arises, (b) it concerns work involving an immediate threat to the
-- health or safety of any person, and (c) given the threat and risk it is not appropriate to adopt the s 73 processes,
-- the employer or the health and safety representative may, after consultation between them, direct that the work cease.
-- JUST FALSE if a condition fails ("if"); NOTHING for anyone else directing (a grant limited in its own wording).
GIVEN `a health or safety issue arose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work involves an immediate threat to health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is not appropriate to use the s 73 process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer and the representative consulted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `who directs` IS A `Who directs`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`work may be directed to cease (s 74)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who directs`
    WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF     `a health or safety issue arose`
           AND `the work involves an immediate threat to health or safety`
           AND `it is not appropriate to use the s 73 process`
           AND `the employer and the representative consulted`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 75(1): if an issue is not resolved under s 73 within a reasonable time, or is the subject of a s 74 direction, any of
-- the parties attempting to resolve it (the employer, the affected employees or their health and safety representative,
-- s 73(1)) may ask the Authority to arrange for an inspector to attend. JUST FALSE if neither condition holds;
-- NOTHING for someone who is not a party.
GIVEN `a party attempting to resolve the issue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not resolved within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subject of a cease-work direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an inspector may be requested (s 75(1))` MEANS
    IF NOT `a party attempting to resolve the issue`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `not resolved within a reasonable time` OR `subject of a cease-work direction`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 75(4): if the inspector (a) issues a prohibition notice or (b) determines in writing that there was reasonable cause
-- for employees to be concerned, an employee who as a result of the issue does not work pending its resolution, but
-- would otherwise be entitled to be paid, continues to be entitled to be paid. JUST FALSE: s 75(4) gives no entitlement
-- on these facts (the conditions are "if").
GIVEN `did not work because of the issue, pending its resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `would otherwise be entitled to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspector issued a prohibition notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspector determined in writing there was reasonable cause for concern` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`pay continues (s 75(4))` MEANS
    IF     (`the inspector issued a prohibition notice` OR `the inspector determined in writing there was reasonable cause for concern`)
       AND `did not work because of the issue, pending its resolution`
       AND `would otherwise be entitled to be paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Discrimination for raising health and safety (ss 76-78E)`

DECLARE `Treatment` IS ONE OF
    `dismissed me`
    `injured me in my employment`
    `altered my position to my detriment`
    `threatened to do one of those things`
    `refused or failed to offer me employment`
    `treated me less favourably than another applicant in offering terms of employment`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Reason` IS ONE OF
    `I am or was a health and safety representative or committee member`
    `I exercised a power as a representative or committee member`
    `I assisted or gave information to an inspector, the Authority, a union authorised representative, a representative or a committee member`
    `I raised a health or safety issue or concern`
    `another reason`

GIVEN `the treatment` IS A `Treatment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is conduct ss 76 and 78A cover` IF
    CONSIDER `the treatment`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Reason`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a listed reason (ss 76(2), 78B(1))` IF
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `another reason` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 78A(1) with s 78B: discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason, where the listed reason is a substantial reason
-- (s 78B(2), a judgment). s 78E(3) defence: the accused proves (a) the conduct was reasonable and (b) a substantial reason
-- was to comply with this Act or the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013.
-- JUST TRUE: a contravention. JUST FALSE: no listed conduct or reason, the reason not substantial (s 78B(2) "may be found
-- ... if"), or the defence proved.
GIVEN `the treatment` IS A `Treatment`
      `the reason` IS A `Reason`
      `the reason was a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a substantial reason was to comply with this Act or the 2013 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78A is contravened` MEANS
    IF     `is conduct ss 76 and 78A cover` `the treatment`
       AND `is a listed reason (ss 76(2), 78B(1))` `the reason`
       AND `the reason was a substantial reason`
       AND (NOT (`the conduct was reasonable` AND `a substantial reason was to comply with this Act or the 2013 Act`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 76(2)-(3): the employer is guilty of an indictable offence if it engaged in the conduct because of a listed reason,
-- and "only if" that reason is the dominant reason (a judgment).
GIVEN `the treatment` IS A `Treatment`
      `the reason` IS A `Reason`
      `the reason was the dominant reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the s 76 offence is made out` MEANS
    IF     `is conduct ss 76 and 78A cover` `the treatment`
       AND `is a listed reason (ss 76(2), 78B(1))` `the reason`
       AND `the reason was the dominant reason`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 78E(1): a proceeding for contravention of s 78A or 78C must be commenced not more than 1 year after the date on
-- which the plaintiff knew or ought to have known that the cause of action accrued.
GIVEN `the day I knew or ought to have known` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to commence a s 78D proceeding (s 78E(1))` MEANS
    `the day` 12 `months after` `the day I knew or ought to have known`

§§ `Prosecutions (ss 131, 132)`

-- s 131(1): a person who considers an occurrence an offence may request in writing that the Authority prosecute if no
-- prosecution has been brought within 6 months of the occurrence. The request may be made from the day after the
-- 6 months end.
GIVEN `the occurrence` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day a s 131 request may be made` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL ((DATE_SERIAL (`the day` 6 `months after` `the occurrence`)) PLUS 1)

-- s 131(2), (2A): within 3 months after receiving the request the Authority must advise (summary offence) or report
-- (indictable offence).
GIVEN `the request was received on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the Authority's reply is due by (s 131(2), (2A))` MEANS
    `the day` 3 `months after` `the request was received on`

-- s 132(1): an indictable offence (other than workplace manslaughter) may be prosecuted within the latest of (a) 2 years
-- after it first comes to the Authority's notice, (b) 1 year after a coronial report or the end of an inquest from which
-- it appeared an offence had been committed, (c) 6 months after a s 16 undertaking is contravened, its contravention
-- comes to the Authority's notice, or its withdrawal is agreed; (d) any time with the DPP's written authorisation.
GIVEN `came to the Authority's notice on` IS A DATE
      `a coronial finding showed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coronial report or inquest ended on` IS A DATE
      `a s 16 undertaking was contravened or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking event was on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the s 132(1) limitation period` MEANS
    `the later of` (`the later of` `limb (a)` `and` `limb (b)`) `and` `limb (c)`
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS `the day` 24 `months after` `came to the Authority's notice on`
        `limb (b)` MEANS IF `a coronial finding showed an offence`
                         THEN `the day` 12 `months after` `the coronial report or inquest ended on`
                         ELSE `limb (a)`
        `limb (c)` MEANS IF `a s 16 undertaking was contravened or withdrawn`
                         THEN `the day` 6 `months after` `the undertaking event was on`
                         ELSE `limb (a)`

§§ `Penalties (Parts 3-5A, 7, 11A, 13; ss 139, 144, 145)`

DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees`
    `s 22(1) employer's duty to monitor and inform`
    `s 22(2) employer's duty to keep records and engage advisers`
    `s 23(1) employer's duty to other persons`
    `s 24(1) self-employed person's duty`
    `s 25(1) employee's duty of care and co-operation`
    `s 25(2) employee's duty not to misuse safety equipment`
    `s 26(1) duty of a person managing or controlling a workplace`
    `s 27(1) designer of plant`
    `s 28(1) designer of buildings or structures`
    `s 29(1) manufacturer of plant or substances`
    `s 30(1) supplier of plant or substances`
    `s 31(1) installer of plant`
    `s 32 reckless endangerment`
    `s 35 duty to consult`
    `s 35A labour hire duty to consult other duty-holders`
    `s 38 incident notification and record`
    `s 39(1) incident site preservation`
    `s 39G(1) workplace manslaughter`
    `s 39G(2) workplace manslaughter by an officer`
    `s 73(2) employer's representative for issue resolution`
    `s 76 discrimination offence`
    `s 148B insuring or indemnifying a penalty`
    `s 153 false or misleading information`

DECLARE `Offender` IS ONE OF
    `a natural person`
    `a body corporate`

-- The maximum fine in penalty units, as each section states it. JUST 0 where the section's penalty is imprisonment
-- only (s 39G(1) for a natural person, s 39G(2)); NOTHING where the section cannot be committed by that kind of offender
-- as written (s 39G(2) by a body corporate).
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
      `the offender` IS AN `Offender`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the maximum fine in penalty units` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` THEN `either` 1800 9000
    WHEN `s 22(1) employer's duty to monitor and inform` THEN `either` 240 1200
    WHEN `s 22(2) employer's duty to keep records and engage advisers` THEN `either` 60 300
    WHEN `s 23(1) employer's duty to other persons` THEN `either` 1800 9000
    WHEN `s 24(1) self-employed person's duty` THEN JUST 1800
    WHEN `s 25(1) employee's duty of care and co-operation` THEN JUST 1800
    WHEN `s 25(2) employee's duty not to misuse safety equipment` THEN JUST 1800
    WHEN `s 26(1) duty of a person managing or controlling a workplace` THEN `either` 1800 9000
    WHEN `s 27(1) designer of plant` THEN `either` 1800 9000
    WHEN `s 28(1) designer of buildings or structures` THEN `either` 500 2500
    WHEN `s 29(1) manufacturer of plant or substances` THEN `either` 1800 9000
    WHEN `s 30(1) supplier of plant or substances` THEN `either` 1800 9000
    WHEN `s 31(1) installer of plant` THEN `either` 1800 9000
    WHEN `s 32 reckless endangerment` THEN `either` 1800 20000
    WHEN `s 35 duty to consult` THEN `either` 180 900
    WHEN `s 35A labour hire duty to consult other duty-holders` THEN `either` 180 900
    WHEN `s 38 incident notification and record` THEN `either` 240 1200
    WHEN `s 39(1) incident site preservation` THEN `either` 240 1200
    WHEN `s 39G(1) workplace manslaughter` THEN `either` 0 100000
    WHEN `s 39G(2) workplace manslaughter by an officer` THEN
         CONSIDER `the offender`
         WHEN `a natural person` THEN JUST 0
         WHEN `a body corporate` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `s 73(2) employer's representative for issue resolution` THEN `either` 60 300
    WHEN `s 76 discrimination offence` THEN `either` 500 2500
    WHEN `s 148B insuring or indemnifying a penalty` THEN `either` 300 1500
    WHEN `s 153 false or misleading information` THEN `either` 240 1200
    WHERE
        `either` `natural` `corporate` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the offender`
            WHEN `a natural person` THEN JUST `natural`
            WHEN `a body corporate` THEN JUST `corporate`

-- The maximum term of imprisonment in years, as each section states it: s 32 (5 years), s 39G(1) and (2) (25 years) for
-- a natural person; JUST 0 where the section states a fine only; NOTHING for a body corporate (it cannot be imprisoned,
-- and the Act does not say so).
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
      `the offender` IS AN `Offender`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offender`
    WHEN `a body corporate` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a natural person` THEN
        CONSIDER `the offence`
        WHEN `s 32 reckless endangerment` THEN JUST 5
        WHEN `s 39G(1) workplace manslaughter` THEN JUST 25
        WHEN `s 39G(2) workplace manslaughter by an officer` THEN JUST 25
        OTHERWISE JUST 0

-- Which offences the Act makes indictable (ss 21(4), 23(2), 24(2), 25(4), 26(3), 27(2)-31(2), 32, 38(6), 39(3),
-- 39G(4), 76(2), 148B(5), 153(3)). ss 22, 35, 35A and 73(2) say nothing, so they are summary offences.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an indictable offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 22(1) employer's duty to monitor and inform` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 22(2) employer's duty to keep records and engage advisers` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 35 duty to consult` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 35A labour hire duty to consult other duty-holders` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 73(2) employer's representative for issue resolution` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Part 3 offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 22(1) employer's duty to monitor and inform` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 22(2) employer's duty to keep records and engage advisers` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 23(1) employer's duty to other persons` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 24(1) self-employed person's duty` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 25(1) employee's duty of care and co-operation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 25(2) employee's duty not to misuse safety equipment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 26(1) duty of a person managing or controlling a workplace` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 27(1) designer of plant` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 28(1) designer of buildings or structures` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 29(1) manufacturer of plant or substances` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 30(1) supplier of plant or substances` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 31(1) installer of plant` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 32 reckless endangerment` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 139(1)-(2): an infringement notice may be an alternative to prosecution only for an offence other than an
-- indictable offence that the regulations prescribe (a fact: the regulations are not deposited), for a penalty not more
-- than the lesser of 10 penalty units and one fifth of the court maximum.
-- JUST the cap; NOTHING where no infringement notice may be served (indictable, or not prescribed).
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
      `the offender` IS AN `Offender`
      `prescribed for infringement notices` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most an infringement notice may specify (s 139(2))` MEANS
    IF `is an indictable offence` `the offence` OR (NOT `prescribed for infringement notices`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the maximum fine in penalty units` `the offence` `the offender`
         WHEN JUST `the maximum` THEN JUST (`the smaller of` 10 `and` (`the maximum` DIVIDED BY 5))
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `Entity` IS ONE OF
    `a body corporate (s 144)`
    `a partnership or unincorporated body or association (s 145)`

-- ss 144(1), 145(1)-(2): an officer is guilty where the entity contravened (for s 145, the duty or offence is the
-- officer's own by subsection (1)) and the contravention is attributable to the officer failing to take reasonable care
-- (a judgment, ss 144(3), 145(4)). An officer who is a volunteer is not liable to be prosecuted for what they did as a
-- volunteer (ss 144(5), 145(5)).
GIVEN `the entity contravened the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `attributable to the officer failing to take reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer acted as a volunteer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the officer is liable (ss 144, 145)` MEANS
    IF `the officer acted as a volunteer`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the entity contravened the provision` AND `attributable to the officer failing to take reasonable care`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- ss 144(1)(a)-(b), 145(3): the officer's maximum fine is 10 000 penalty units where the provision is s 39G(1), and
-- otherwise the maximum fine for a natural person for the same provision.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the officer's maximum fine in penalty units (ss 144(1), 145(3))` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 39G(1) workplace manslaughter` THEN JUST 10000
    WHEN `s 39G(2) workplace manslaughter by an officer` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE `the maximum fine in penalty units` `the offence` `a natural person`

§§ `Regulative rules`

DECLARE `OHS party` IS ONE OF
    `the duty-holder`
    `the Authority`
    `the person who asked`

DECLARE `OHS act` IS ONE OF
    `give the Authority a written record of the incident`
    `report in writing to the person who made the request`
    `wait`

-- s 38(3): within 48 hours after being required to notify the Authority, the employer or self-employed person must
-- also give it a written record of the incident. Clock: hours from the moment the duty to notify arose.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `OHS party` `OHS act`
`s 38(3) -- the written record of the incident within 48 hours` MEANS
    PARTY `the duty-holder`
    MUST  `give the Authority a written record of the incident`
    WITHIN 48
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the duty-holder` BECAUSE "s 38(3): no written record of the incident was given to the Authority within 48 hours after the duty to notify arose (an offence under s 38(5): 240 penalty units for a natural person, 1200 for a body corporate)"

-- s 131(2), (2A): within 3 months after receiving a s 131(1) request, the Authority must advise or report in writing to
-- the person who made it. Clock: days; the period is the number of days from receipt to the same day 3 months later.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `OHS party` `OHS act`
`s 131(2) -- the Authority must report to the person who asked within 3 months` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the Authority`
    MUST  `report in writing to the person who made the request`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Authority` BECAUSE "s 131(2), (2A): the Authority did not advise or report in writing within 3 months after receiving the request; the person may ask that the matter be referred to the Director of Public Prosecutions once the Authority has not prosecuted within 9 months (s 131(3))"
